    </nav>
    <a class="btn printhide" href="#contact">Get a quote</a>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ═══ HERO ═══ -->
<div class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="year-tag">EDITION 2026 · PAKISTAN</div>
    <h1>Commercial plaza design &amp; construction, <em>priced floor by floor.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">2026 plaza construction rates and a live estimator for any city and any society — DHA, Bahria Town, LDA, CDA or a private scheme. Enter your plot, basements and floors as your bylaws allow; the covered area, cost, programme and payment schedule follow.</p>

    <div class="rates">
      <div class="rate">
        <div class="lbl">Gray structure — above ground</div>
        <div class="val">Rs 3,700<small>/ SFT</small></div>
        <div class="sub">RCC frame for commercial loads and 20–30 ft spans, stair and lift core, masonry, plaster, roof and parapet.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rate">
        <div class="lbl">Basement — gray structure</div>
        <div class="val">Rs 6,500<small>/ SFT</small></div>
        <div class="sub">Excavation, shoring, RCC retaining walls, raft, waterproofing and dewatering.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rate opt">
        <div class="lbl">Finishing</div>
        <div class="val">Rs 1,900<small>/ SFT SHELL &amp; CORE</small></div>
        <div class="val">Rs 3,000<small>/ SFT STANDARD</small></div>
        <div class="sub">Premium Rs 5,500 / SFT. Lahore base rates — the estimator adjusts for your city.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="citystrip">
      <b>Cities served</b>
      <span>Lahore · Islamabad · Rawalpindi · Karachi · Faisalabad · Multan · Gujranwala · Sialkot · Peshawar · and all major cities of Pakistan</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══ INTRODUCTION ═══ -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">About this guide</p>
    <h2>What moves the cost of a plaza</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">A plaza is not priced on one covered-area figure. Each floor is measured against the bylaws of your society, the basement is priced on its own, and lifts, fire safety and facade are sized to the building. The rates are 2026 market estimates for standard commercial work; every ACCO project is confirmed with a measured BOQ.</p>

    <div class="grid3">
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 01</div><h4>Society bylaws</h4><p>Each authority sets its own coverage, floors and height — DHA by plot and phase, LDA by zone and road width, CDA by floor area ratio.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 02</div><h4>Basement</h4><p>A full-plot basement with shoring, retaining walls and waterproofing costs about 75% more per SFT than above ground.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 03</div><h4>Number of floors</h4><p>Taller buildings need shear walls, higher concrete grades and more lifts, pushing the gray rate toward the high end.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 04</div><h4>City</h4><p>Rock strata in Islamabad, saline soil and a high water table in Karachi, and freight on finishes all shift the rate.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 05</div><h4>Facade</h4><p>ACP, glass or stone frontage. A glass curtain wall can cost more per SFT of facade than the floor behind it.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 06</div><h4>Lifts and fire safety</h4><p>Lifts, fire alarm, hose reels, sprinklers and pumps are priced as add-ons, sized to the building.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 07</div><h4>Finishing level</h4><p>Shell &amp; core leaves units bare for tenants. Standard and premium finishing complete every unit.</p></div>
      <div class="cell"><div class="n">FACTOR 08</div><h4>Ground conditions</h4><p>Water table, soil strength and neighbouring buildings decide shoring, piling and dewatering.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══ ESTIMATOR ═══ -->
<section class="tint" id="estimator">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Live estimator</p>
    <h2>Price your plaza</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Choose your city and society, enter the plot, then set the basements, floors and mezzanine your bylaws allow. Coverage rules fill in for the society you pick and can be changed to match your approved plan.</p>

    <div class="est">
      <div class="est-controls">
        <div class="field">
          <span class="ctrl-label">Location</span>
          <div class="grid2">
            <div><label class="mini" for="citySel">City</label><select class="sel" id="citySel"></select></div>
            <div><label class="mini" for="authSel">Society / authority</label><select class="sel" id="authSel"></select></div>
          </div>
          <input type="text" id="qSociety" class="txt" style="margin-top:8px" placeholder="Society or scheme name — e.g. DHA Phase 6, Bahria Orchard, Gulberg">
          <div class="note-box" id="authNote"></div>
        </div>

        <label class="ctrl-label" id="plotlabel">Plot size</label>
        <div class="chips" role="group" aria-labelledby="plotlabel" id="plotChips"></div>
        <div class="field">
          <div class="grid2">
            <div><label class="mini" for="cW">Frontage (ft)</label><input type="number" id="cW" min="10" max="600" step="any" value="30" inputmode="decimal"></div>
            <div><label class="mini" for="cD">Depth (ft)</label><input type="number" id="cD" min="10" max="600" step="any" value="60" inputmode="decimal"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="plotarea" id="plotArea">—</div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <span class="ctrl-label">Floors — as your bylaws allow</span>
          <div class="counts">
            <div><span class="mini">Basements</span>
              <div class="stepper" data-k="b"><button type="button" data-d="-1" aria-label="Fewer basements">−</button><input type="number" id="vB" min="0" max="5" step="1" inputmode="numeric" aria-label="Number of basements"><button type="button" data-d="1" aria-label="More basements">+</button></div>
            </div>
            <div><span class="mini">Upper floors</span>
              <div class="stepper" data-k="u"><button type="button" data-d="-1" aria-label="Fewer upper floors">−</button><input type="number" id="vU" min="0" max="60" step="1" inputmode="numeric" aria-label="Number of upper floors"><button type="button" data-d="1" aria-label="More upper floors">+</button></div>
            </div>
            <div><span class="mini">Mezzanine</span>
              <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Mezzanine" id="mezSeg">
                <button type="button" data-v="1" aria-pressed="true">Included</button>
                <button type="button" data-v="0">Not included</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <label class="chkline"><input type="checkbox" id="lmrChk" checked> Lift machine room (75 SFT)</label>
          <div class="hint" id="cfgHint"></div>
          <div class="advice" id="bylawAdvice"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <span class="ctrl-label">Coverage rules <span style="text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;color:#8B9AAE">— from your society's bylaws, edit if yours differ</span></span>
          <div class="grid3c">
            <div><label class="ctrl-label" for="cvB">Basement % of plot</label><input type="number" id="cvB" min="0" max="100" step="any" inputmode="decimal"></div>
            <div><label class="ctrl-label" for="cvG">Ground % of plot</label><input type="number" id="cvG" min="0" max="100" step="any" inputmode="decimal"></div>
            <div><label class="ctrl-label" for="cvU">Upper floors % of plot</label><input type="number" id="cvU" min="0" max="100" step="any" inputmode="decimal"></div>
            <div><label class="ctrl-label" for="cvM">Mezzanine %</label><input type="number" id="cvM" min="0" max="100" step="any" inputmode="decimal"></div>
            <div><label class="ctrl-label" for="cvV">Verandah depth (ft)</label><input type="number" id="cvV" min="0" max="30" step="any" inputmode="decimal"></div>
            <div><label class="ctrl-label" for="cvMt">Stair mumty (SFT)</label><input type="number" id="cvMt" min="0" max="2000" step="any" inputmode="decimal"></div>
