<!-- ═══ FAQ ═══ -->
<section class="tint" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
    <h2>Commercial plaza costs, answered</h2>

    <div class="faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>How much does an 8 Marla commercial plaza cost?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>Taking a DHA Lahore Phase V plaza built to B+G+M+4F as the example — <span id="fq1a">—</span> including basement, mumty and lift machine room — gray structure is about <span id="fq1g">—</span>. Shell &amp; core comes to about <span id="fq1s">—</span>, and standard turnkey finishing to about <span id="fq1t">—</span>, at Lahore rates. Lifts, fire systems and facade upgrades are extra. Use the estimator for your own society's floors.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>And a 4 Marla plaza?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>A 4 Marla B+G+M+4F plaza with <span id="fq2a">—</span> of covered area costs about <span id="fq2g">—</span> for gray structure and <span id="fq2t">—</span> with standard turnkey finishing, at Lahore rates.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do rates differ between Lahore, Islamabad and Karachi?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>Yes. Islamabad and Rawalpindi run about 5–10% higher on gray structure and 10–20% higher on basements because of boulder and rock strata. Karachi runs about 5–10% lower on gray structure but 10–25% higher on basements near the coast, where the water table is high and soil is saline. The estimator applies these when you choose your city.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How many floors can I build on my commercial plot?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>It depends on the society. In DHA Lahore, 4 and 8 Marla plots are allowed B+G+M+2F (52 ft) in Phases I–IV and B+G+M+4F (74/78 ft) from Phase V. LDA commercial centres allow B+G+5 on 4–8 Marla and B+G+6 on 1 Kanal. CDA controls commercial plots by floor area ratio rather than floor count, and Bahria Town sets floors per plot through its Design Wing. Enter the floors on your approved plan in the estimator.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why is commercial more expensive per square foot than a house?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>Heavier floor loads, larger column-free spans, a full-plot basement with shoring and waterproofing, and taller buildings with lift and fire requirements. Expect gray structure to run 20–30% above residential rates.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is the basement worth it?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>On a small plot a basement adds 900–1,800 SFT of rentable or storage area at about Rs 9,500 per SFT finished for shops (Rs 6,500 gray plus Rs 3,000 finishing), against about Rs 6,700 per SFT above ground. It pays when basement rents are at least 50–60% of ground-floor rents.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Should I build shell &amp; core or fully finished?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>Shell &amp; core saves about Rs 1,100 per SFT against standard finishing and lets tenants fit out to their own brand. Full finishing rents faster for small offices. Many owners finish the common areas and washrooms and leave units bare.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How long will it take?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>For an 8 Marla B+G+M+4F plaza: three to four months of design and approval, then about <span id="fq7">—</span> from mobilisation to handover with standard finishing.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need parking?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>It depends on the authority. DHA 4–32 Marla plots rely on frontage parking, with basement parking mandatory above 4 Kanal. LDA asks for one car per 1,600 SFT on larger commercial plots, and Bahria Town byelaws one car per 1,000 SFT where the layout provides none.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What is not in the per-square-foot rate?</summary>
        <div class="ans"><p>Design fees, approvals, utilities, lifts, generator, HVAC, fire pumps and sprinklers, curtain walls and tenant fit-outs. Budget 15–30% on top of the construction rate for a fully serviced plaza, or select the add-ons in the estimator to price them.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

